Article 34

1. The Unit Task for the Protection of Women and Children at the Village/Sub-District Level as referred to in Article 31 letter c, constitutes a functional work unit that organizes integrated protection services and handling of cases of violence against children and women at the Village/Sub-District level.
2. The Management of the Unit Task for the Protection of Women and Children at the Village/Sub-District Level as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. elements of Village/Sub-District apparatus;
b. elements of Village Non-Commissioned Officer (Babinsa)/Sub-District;
c. elements of Community Non-Commissioned Officer (Babinmas);
d. community leaders/religious leaders;
e. youth elements; and
f. elements of the Village/Sub-District PKK Driving Team
3. The main duties of the Unit Task for the Protection of Women and Children at the Village/Sub-District Level as referred to in paragraph (1) are:
a. providing services in the context of protecting women and children;
b. receiving public complaints regarding cases of violence against women and children in the Village/Sub-District area;
c. facilitating women and children who are victims of violence in resolving their problems;
d. socializing to the community about the protection of women and children; and
e. providing assistance to victims or referring to the task force for the protection of women and children at the Sub-District level.
4. Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties and functions of the Unit Task for the Protection of Women and Children at the Village/Sub-District Level as referred to in paragraph (1), are stipulated by Village Head/Sub-District Head's Decree.

